gree Programs Application Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe International Students During Studies Start Studies During Studies During Studies Student Organizations Intranet After Studies Start Studies After Studies After Studies Organizational Matters Master and Doctorate Starting Work Staying in Touch KIT Departments Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Start Studies Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living in Karlsruhe Learning at the KIT Transportation Research Start Research Research Topics Start Research Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Excellence Start Research Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Helmholtz Programs Research Networks Start Research Research Networks Research Networks Collaborative Research Centers DFG Research Units Young Scientists Start Research Young Scientists Young Scientists Doctorate Start Research Young Scientists Doctorate Doctorate Doing a Doctorate at KIT Doctoral Programs Postdoc Phase Paths to Professorship Start Research Young Scientists Paths to Professorship Paths to Professorship Young Investigator Group Preparation Program KIT-Nachwuchsgruppe KIT Associate Fellow Tenure-track Professorship Research Infrastructures Security Research Scientific Integrity Innovation Start Innovation Innovation Technology Transfer Cooperation Innovation in Academic Education and Research Starting a Business Career Start Career Career Working at KIT Start Career Working at KIT Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment KIT for International Talent Get Started Start Career Get Started Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Application Process Start Career Application Process Application Process FAQ Jobs Startpage Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Your Career at KIT A Career at KIT means shaping the Future: Together, Diversely, and Effectively. Whether in science, infrastructure, administration, or education – every perspective counts for us. Around 10,000 employees and 23,000 students pursue one common goal: To make an impact. What connects us is respect, commitment, diversity, and our curiosity about tomorrow. Welcome to a working environment where your ideas count. Amadeus Bramsiepe, KIT Working at KIT Flexible working hours and family-friendly policies to a retirement provision plan, at KIT we see security as reliable working conditions, opportunities for development, and a strong sense of community. What really matters to us is that you can thrive. We create an environment in which people feel secure, are allowed to ask questions, take responsibility, and courageously break new ground. In teams that embrace diversity and share responsibility. Working at KIT allows you to balance your professional and private life according to your individual life concept. Working at KIT Magali Hauser, KIT Start Your Career Whether you are looking for an apprenticeship, a cooperative study program, a career start, or the next step in your scientific career, at KIT you will find many paths to your goal. We support what drives you – with prospects, trust, and room to grow. Get Started Magali Hauser, KIT International Diversity KIT welcomes international talent with multilingual welcome services and an open atmosphere. We provide support during onboarding and beyond, including assistance with finding accommodation, language courses, and collaboration in intercultural teams and international projects. Because we see intercultural experience as a strength. KIT for Internationals Magali Hauser, KIT Our Application Process At KIT your application begins with a clear, transparent process and comprehensive support. Because we know that an application is the first step toward a shared future. Application Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers Any Questions? Our FAQs offer tips and answers on everything related to applying and getting started. View FAQs Insights into Our Work Culture We take responsibility, think ahead, and shape the future together. Get to Know Our Work Culture Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Media Press Releases Contact for Media Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
