      "title": "We Create Impact – Because Every Perspective Helps Us Move Forward",
      "description": "Diversity | KIT KIT - Karlsruhe Institute of Technology image/svg+xml Karlsruhe Institute of Technology skip navigation Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT de search search KIT Start KIT KIT Profile Start KIT Profile Profile Vision Excellence Start KIT Profile Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Equal Opportunities and Diversity Sustainability Data and Facts Start KIT Profile Data and Facts Data and Facts Rankings Organization Start KIT Organization Organization Management Bodies and Committees Start KIT Organization Bodies and Committees Bodies and Committees Supervisory Board Executive Board Heads of Divisions KIT Senate Convention Staff Representation Students Union Divisions Start KIT Organization Divisions Divisions Institutes KIT Departments HGF Programs KIT Centers Administration and Infrastructure Project Management Agency Karlsruhe People Start KIT People People Personalities History Top-level Researchers Start KIT People Top-level Researchers Top-level Researchers Alexander von Humboldt Foundation AvH European Research Council German Research Foundation Getting Involved Start KIT Getting Involved Getting Involved KIT GIVING KIT Foundation Sponsoring KIT Alumni KFG Media Start KIT Media Media Press Releases Start KIT Media Press Releases Press Releases PI 2026 Archive Press Releases News Start KIT Media News News News 2026 Highlight Topics Newly Appointed Annual Report Publications Campus Life Start KIT Campus Life Campus Life 200 Years of KIT KIT for All Campus Tours Events Start KIT Campus Life Events Events Events Calendar Locations Start KIT Locations Locations Interactive Campus Map Maps for Download Topics Start Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Studies Start Studies Studies Prior to Studies Start Studies Prior to Studies Prior to Studies Degree Programs Application Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe International Students During Studies Start Studies During Studies During Studies Student Organizations Intranet After Studies Start Studies After Studies After Studies Organizational Matters Master and Doctorate Starting Work Staying in Touch KIT Departments Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Start Studies Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living in Karlsruhe Learning at the KIT Transportation Research Start Research Research Topics Start Research Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Excellence Start Research Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Helmholtz Programs Research Networks Start Research Research Networks Research Networks Collaborative Research Centers DFG Research Units Young Scientists Start Research Young Scientists Young Scientists Doctorate Start Research Young Scientists Doctorate Doctorate Doing a Doctorate at KIT Doctoral Programs Postdoc Phase Paths to Professorship Start Research Young Scientists Paths to Professorship Paths to Professorship Young Investigator Group Preparation Program KIT-Nachwuchsgruppe KIT Associate Fellow Tenure-track Professorship Research Infrastructures Security Research Scientific Integrity Innovation Start Innovation Innovation Technology Transfer Cooperation Innovation in Academic Education and Research Starting a Business Career Start Career Career Working at KIT Start Career Working at KIT Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment KIT for International Talent Get Started Start Career Get Started Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Application Process Start Career Application Process Application Process FAQ Jobs Startpage Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Working at KIT Diversity Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment Diversity We Create Impact – Because Every Perspective Helps Us Move Forward At KIT, we consciously promote diversity through respect, openness, and fair conditions. Different perspectives and experiences make us stronger through collaboration. We want everyone at KIT to be able to develop their potential and feel like they belong. As a signatory to the Charta der Vielfalt (Diversity Charter), we stand for equal opportunities – diversity is part of our identity. We particularly empower people who are still underrepresented in science, which includes women, and promote diversity across all genders and identities. Our teams are interdisciplinary, our paths are individual, and our attitude is clear: Every perspective counts. Equal Opportunities and Diversity 90% think that it is enriching to work in a diverse team 70% feel like they belong at KIT KIT Diversity Dashboard \"My experience in an international research group showed me how diverse perspectives help reduce bias and lead to better scientific research .“ Patricia Guerra Balboa Doctoral Researcher \"What I love most about my job is helping people and seeing how grateful they are.\" Johann Seemayer Representative of Disabled Employees \"I find working with international students and staff highly motivating, especially when we collaborate to create new programs together.” Nur Bakkar Project Coordinator Welcome and Integration Diversity Has Many Forms and One Common Attitude What connects us is more than just a workplace: It is our conviction that diversity is an asset. When people with different backgrounds come together, they develop solutions that are more innovative, bold, and sustainable. Support through Services Tailored to Different Stages of Life From (emergency) childcare to starting a family and school vacations to caring for relatives: We provide support in many individual life situations. Familiy and Elder Care Values in Everyday Life: Respect and Appreciation Training on unconscious bias, intercultural exchange formats, and offerings for building diversity competence strengthen mutual respect and awareness. Trainings Inclusive and Supportive Through understanding and appropriate support, we take into account the different needs of people with (severe) disabilities and chronic illnesses and create accessible structures for active participation. Representatives of Disabled Employees (website in German) Mental and Physical Health Whether you are working or studying, we care about your well-being and support your development.en. Health Network (website in German) Developing Together We are committed to equal opportunities and diversity with structures and offerings that strengthen intercultural exchange and develop diversity skills. Gender and Diversity Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: KIT for Internationals Female Scientists at KIT Benefits Work Culture Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-07-09 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
