acy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Working at KIT Benefits Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment Benefits Our Benefits At KIT, people shape the future – with ideas, commitment, and expertise. To help you develop your strengths, we offer benefits that count:  From career-family balance to health promotion and continued education to personal development. As a public-sector employer, we create reliable conditions. If you want to help shape the future in technology, administration, science, or teaching, you will find a meaningful work environment with great prospects at KIT. 82% find that their work at KIT is compatible with their personal life situation Career and Development Grow with Prospects – Your Professional Development at KIT Whether you are just starting out or looking to advance your career, at KIT you will grow with us. We promote your strengths, accompany you on new paths, and create space for your individual development, taking into account different professional backgrounds and learning paths. Wide Range of Continued Education Opportunities at KIT Whether in terms of technical, methodological, or personal development, The Human Resources Development Business Unit (PEBA) and the Center for Advanced Technological and Environmental Training (FTU) support you with a wide range of consulting services, development tools, seminars, and courses. Individual Development Opportunities – From Career Entry to Leadership We accompany you throughout your entire career path: From structured onboarding and individual qualification measures to management qualification programs . Support for Dissertation Projects For research assistants, we offer structured dissertation programs, individual supervision, and interdisciplinary opportunities for further scientific qualification. The Karlsruhe House of Young Scientists (KHYS) is the central point of contact for those interested in pursuing a dissertation, doctoral candidates, and postdocs – offering comprehensive advice, qualification opportunities, and networking formats. Health and Wellbeing Stay Healthy – with Comprehensive Support You can only be effective if you feel well. That's why we strengthen your health – physically and mentally. With offers that are suitable for everyday use and take different needs into account, because good ideas need a good foundation. FIT at KIT – Health Promotion in the Workplace Under the motto “Fit at KIT – with Body, Mind, and Soul,” we promote your health holistically: With active breaks, back training, sports courses, mental health services, personal training, and regular preventive medical checkups. Visit our Health Network for an overview (in German). Medical Check-ups and Consultations In addition to occupational health examinations, we offer voluntary preventive care services. Influenza vaccinations, colorectal cancer screening, and individual medical consultations are available through our Medical Services (MED) (website only available in German). KIT Sports Program – Exercise and Balance Whether you prefer functional training, yoga, climbing, or soccer, the KIT Sports Program offers over 80 sports options for every fitness level. Many courses take place directly on campus. Discover all sports facilities at KIT (in German) – from university sports to the KIT Sports Club. Culture and Community Shaping Things Together – Experiencing KIT KIT is more than just a workplace – it is a place where ideas meet exchange and diversity meets creativity. Whether it's a choir, theater, or initiative, our cultural programs create space for encounters and personal connections. Cultural Programs at KIT From concerts by the Academic Orchestra to exhibitions and readings to the KIT Chamber Choir: We offer a wide range of cultural activities (in German) that you can actively participate in or simply relax and enjoy. Get Involved and Actively Participate Whether music, art, or theater – many cultural offerings (in German) at KIT thrive on the commitment of employees and students. Get involved, exchange ideas, and actively participate. Events And Exchange Formats Regular events such as Science Night, Diversity Day, and lecture series invite you to engage in interdisciplinary dialogue. You can find upcoming events in our events calendar . Work-life Integration Live And Work in Balance – in a Flexible And Family-friendly Environment Your life is multifaceted, and we make room for that. Whether for family, caregiving responsibilities, or personal projects: With flexibility, family friendliness, and a sensitivity to diverse life concepts – including single parents and queer family models – we create working conditions that take your needs into account. For more balance in everyday life. Flexible Working Hours And Working Models Whether you are an early bird or a night owl – we offer you flexible working hours. With flexitime, part-time options, and the possibility of working remotely up to 80% of the time, you can organize your work flexibly, adapted to your life situation and your respective area of responsibility. Various Offers for Families And Childcare Whether you are on parental leave, caring for relatives, or looking for childcare: As part of our services for families at KIT, we support you with many offers to help you balance your career and family life. These include: Advice on family and care responsibilities KIT daycare centers for various age groups located close to the campus Vacation programs and short-term childcare solutions A parent-child office with PC workstations and child-friendly equipment for emergencies KIT Family Portal with more information. In addition, the “Families at KIT” network provides opportunities for exchange, practical tips, and up-to-date information on dates and offers. 30 Days of Vacation – Plus Special Leave and Days Off We offer you 30 vacation days per year. In addition, there is special leave for special life situations, and on December 24 and 31, you have time off in accordance with the collective agreement (Tarifvereinbarung), giving you more time with family and friends. Remuneration And Financial Benefits Transparent Pay – With Attractive Additional Benefits It is not only your salary that counts, but also what lasts. At KIT, you benefit from transparent remuneration in the public sector and additional benefits that provide you with peace of mind, security, and a foundation for the future. Company Pension Plan (VBL) – Security for Your Future To ensure that you are well provided for in retirement, you will receive a company pension plan through the VBL (Versorgungsanstalt des Bundes und der Länder) in addition to your statutory pension. JobTicket Subsidy or Discounted Deutschland-Ticket We support environmentally friendly mobility: You benefit from a monthly subsidy of 25 euros for the JobTicket BW. Annual Special Payments in Accordance with Collective Agreement In addition to your monthly salary, you receive an additional special payment – regulated in accordance with the applicable collective agreement provisions. Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: Work Culture Dversity Working Environment Application Process Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-07-09 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
