Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Working at KIT Working Environment Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment Working Environment The Working Environment at KIT Our Locations: Well-connected, Green, and Integrated From Campus South in the heart of Karlsruhe to Campus North in Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen, we offer modern, easily accessible infrastructure, short distances, and a vibrant community. In Karlsruhe, we also conduct research at Campus East near the Technologiepark and at Campus West in the Nordweststadt district. Beyond Karlsruhe, KIT is present in Ulm, Garmisch-Partenkirchen, and Dresden. All locations have one thing in common: They create space for ideas, exchange, and the inspiring feeling of making an impact together. Working in Karlsruhe KIT Location Advantages in Karlsruhe Our Karlsruhe locations are very well connected, with short distances and flexible mobility options designed to fit your daily routine. The free KIT Shuttle connects Campus South, North, and East quickly and reliably. In addition, dedicated buses for KIT staff from surrounding communities make it easier to commute to Campus North in the mornings and afternoons. Karlsruhe is a cycling city: Well-developed cycle paths, ample parking options, and short distances often make cycling the fastest means of transport. We also promote climate-friendly mobility with EV charging stations at all Karlsruhe locations and discounted JobTickets. The KIT Library, located at several different sites , gives you access to knowledge, research, and digital resources. Our Mensa , canteens , and several cafés provide a wide range of food options right on campus. We also support parents with reliable childcare offerings that help simplify everyday life. Campus Overview in Karlsruhe KIT Campus South – Urban, Lively, Integrated Central location in the heart of Karlsruhe Direct access to the Schlossgarten (palace gardens): green and open Excellent connections to bus, rail, and the KIT Shuttle International campus community with students from all over the world Canteens, cafés, and modern infrastructure A vibrant link between teaching, research, and city life KIT Campus North – Research-driven, Scenic, Well Connected Large-scale research campus (approx. 2 km²) in Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen Easy to reach by KIT Shuttle, Campus Transport, and e-mobility options On site canteen and diverse working environment Quiet spaces for focused work as well as hubs for collaboration Unique scientific infrastructure enabling groundbreaking research Other KIT Locations Beyond Campus South and Campus North, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology operates at several additional locations – each with its own research profile, regional connections, and specialized areas of expertise. Campus East (Karlsruhe Rintheim): Mobility, mechanical engineering, process automation Campus West (Nordweststadt Karlsruhe): Institutes across a broad range of disciplines Garmisch Partenkirchen : Institute of Meteorology and Climate Research, atmospheric environmental research with a focus on climate change Ulm : Helmholtz Institute Ulm for Electrochemical Energy Storage Dresden : Branch office of the Project Management Agency Karlsruhe, scientific project funding All KIT Locations and Directions Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: Work Culture Dversity Benefits Application Process Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
