Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career KIT for International Talent Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs KIT for International Talent KIT for International Talent Are you from abroad and would like to work, pursue a doctorate, teach, or conduct research in Germany? Then KIT is the right place for you. We warmly welcome people from all over the world and value the diverse experiences, perspectives, and life paths that enrich our international community. Our Welcome Service is the central service point for international researchers, academic teachers, doctoral candidates, and their families. We support you in planning and organizing your stay and offer comprehensive information, advice, and support before your arrival in Germany, for example on issues such as visas and relocation. Our lively campus life connects people: With a wide range of events and open meeting spaces, you will quickly make new friends. The city of Karlsruhe combines technology, cosmopolitanism, culture, and quality of life. At KIT, you will find space to settle in, get involved, and develop personally and professionally . Why Work in Germany? Germany is one of the most attractive countries to live and work in, offering career opportunities and further training possibilities combined with a high quality of life. We support you in getting started while taking into account different life situations. Magali Hauser, KIT A Strong Economy and Secure Jobs Work in Europe's largest economy, with reliable employment conditions and an innovation-driven environment. At KIT, you can expect long-term prospects in public service and excellent research projects with reliable funding. Fair Remuneration and Social Benefits You can expect fair pay and comprehensive social benefits, including health, nursing care, and unemployment insurance as well as a pension scheme. In addition, KIT offers supplementary occupational pension provision (VBL) and transparent regulations. Work-Life-Integration Regulated working hours, generous vacation time, and opportunities for mobile work. At KIT, we offer flexible models that take different life situations into account, such as family, caregiving responsibilities, and personal projects. Health and Wellbeing Access to high-quality medical care. KIT's Medical Services (MED) offer occupational health services and counseling. Cities Worth Living in Modern infrastructure, short distances, and a high level of safety characterize Germany as a whole and the city of Karlsruhe in particular. With its green campus, good public transport connections, and bicycle-friendly environment, KIT offers a high quality of life in one of Europe's most livable and economically strongest regions. Cultural Diversity Centrally located in Europe, Germany offers many travel and exchange opportunities. At KIT, you will find international networks, events, and community formats, a multilingual environment, as well as international teams and working groups. Welcome Culture International professionals and their families benefit from dedicated support programs. In addition, KIT offers welcome services, relocation support, onboarding in English/German, and community events. \" Germany has many great services that I didn’t have in my home country, especially childcare for families moving here with young children. \" Marufa Sultana Scientist \"Language won’t be a problem – English is widely used at German universities. You can build a strong international network and benefit from strong engineering expertise.\" Gan Huang Head of Junior Research Group \"I was really pleasantly surprised to see so many people from different countries bringing their culture and knowledge with them.\" Lízia Maria Goncalves Branco Doctoral Researcher Working Environment in Karlsruhe Karlsruhe combines career opportunities, joie de vivre, and a smooth everyday life. The city offers a dynamic technological scene, nature, culture, and short, barrier-free distances , making it perfect for anyone who thinks globally and wants to settle locally. Get to know our locations and discover what makes the “Fächerstadt”, our fan-shaped city, special for international talent. Working Environment Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: Benefits Application Process Work Culture Diversity Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
