rivacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Get Started Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Your Start at KIT Opportunities for Every Stage of Your Career You are looking to make a fresh start, gain initial professional experience, or develop your career in a specific direction? We will support you with programs, guidance, and perspectives that are practically relevant, future-oriented, and meaningful. We create an environment in which people feel secure, are allowed to ask questions, take responsibility, and courageously break new ground. Markus Breig, KIT Conduct research, teach, and transfer knowledge: Shape innovation in interdisciplinary teams with modern infrastructure and clear career paths. Science Amadeus Bramsiepe, KIT Technology, maintenance, and security: Keep our campuses  running, with responsible roles and a reliable work environment. Infrastructure KIT Processes, service, and strategy: Support research and teaching with organizational talent, teamwork, and development opportunities. Administration Magali Hauser, KIT Combine theory and practice: Launch your career with vocational training or a cooperative study program. Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Magali Hauser, KIT Get involved and gain experience: Get to know KIT from a professional perspective as a student assistant, through an internship, or while working on your thesis. Students KIT Spark curiosity and nurture talent: Discover programs and opportunities for young people – from workshops to pupils laboratories (in German). Children and Teens Career Paths at KIT From entry-level positions to specialist and leadership roles. Learn about our Career Paths Insights into Our Work Culture We take responsibility, 