cy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Get Started Science Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Science A Research Career at KIT Research today. Change tomorrow. Together at KIT. Become part of a unique institution that combines academic teaching with large-scale national research – open, excellent, and interdisciplinary. We provide targeted support through programs, networks, and clear paths for development at every stage of your career. Our environment integrates basic research with practical application, thereby enabling pioneering work and interdisciplinary projects. At KIT, international researchers will find structures that foster orientation, integration, and equality – from entry-level positions all the way to a professorship. Laila Tkotz, KIT Conduct research at a university of excellence with creative freedom and societal relevance. Professorship: Appointment and Career Markus Breig, KIT Take on responsibility, test your own ideas, and explore new approaches – in an environment that offers security and support and promotes innovation. Leadership of a Junior Research Group or Junior Professorship Markus Breig, KIT Expand your research, strengthen your professional network, and prepare for the next step in your career with tailored support. Postdoc KIT Obtain your doctorate in an inspiring environment with excellent guidance, a strong network, and on equal footing. Doctorate Conducting Research at KIT As the University in the Helmholtz Association, we combine academic teaching with the infrastructure of a large-scale research institution. Together, we develop solutions to major challenges such as climate change, the energy transition, future mobility, and artificial intelligence. We offer well-connected structures and an environment where new ideas can flourish, supported by the Excellence Strategy and Helmholtz programs. Women in Science We particularly empower wome in science and promote diversity across all genders and identities. Female Scientists at KIT KIT Attractive Conditions for Your Research At KIT, you will find dependable structures to support your career and sufficient space for your research, such as professorships with reduced teaching loads (two hours per week). Even without a professorship, you have the opportunity to expand your scope of responsibility as you gain experience, for example by taking on leadership roles. In addition, tenured researchers at KIT have attractive career opportunities beyond the professorship. Tenure-track Professorship Career Paths beyond Professorships Experience diversity – Shape your career We always keep your international mobility and personal development in mind. Promoting equal opportunity and diversity, we create transparent support processes at every stage of your career, such as initiatives to balance work and personal life and targeted counseling on dual careers. Balancing Work and Personal Life Equal Opportunities and Diversity Appointment Procedures Dual Career Service Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: Benefits Diversity Working Environment Work Culture Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
