Studies Prior to Studies Prior to Studies Degree Programs Application Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe International Students During Studies Start Studies During Studies During Studies Student Organizations Intranet After Studies Start Studies After Studies After Studies Organizational Matters Master and Doctorate Starting Work Staying in Touch KIT Departments Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Start Studies Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living in Karlsruhe Learning at the KIT Transportation Research Start Research Research Topics Start Research Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Excellence Start Research Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Helmholtz Programs Research Networks Start Research Research Networks Research Networks Collaborative Research Centers DFG Research Units Young Scientists Start Research Young Scientists Young Scientists Doctorate Start Research Young Scientists Doctorate Doctorate Doing a Doctorate at KIT Doctoral Programs Postdoc Phase Paths to Professorship Start Research Young Scientists Paths to Professorship Paths to Professorship Young Investigator Group Preparation Program KIT-Nachwuchsgruppe KIT Associate Fellow Tenure-track Professorship Research Infrastructures Security Research Scientific Integrity Innovation Start Innovation Innovation Technology Transfer Cooperation Innovation in Academic Education and Research Starting a Business Career Start Career Career Working at KIT Start Career Working at KIT Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment KIT for International Talent Get Started Start Career Get Started Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Application Process Start Career Application Process Application Process FAQ Jobs Startpage Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Get Started Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Choose from over 25 vocational training programs in industrial-technical, natural sciences, business, and IT fields, as well as 12 cooperative study programs: Start your career with hands-on experience, remuneration, and excellent prospects. Every year, around 100 young people begin their training at KIT. In our cooperative study programs, in partnership with the Baden-Württemberg Cooperative State University, and our vocational training, you will be involved in real projects. You will gain a wide range of skills that are in demand in the professional world and earn a Bachelor of Arts, Bachelor of Science, or Bachelor of Engineering degree. You are also welcome  to join us if you have an international high school diploma or a multilingual background. Magali Hauser, KIT Vocational Training at KIT Learn through hands-on experience, help shape projects as part of a team, and build strong skills – right at the heart of research. Vocational Training Programs KIT Cooperative Study Programs at DHBW Alternating theory and practice, fair compensation , and real project work across twelve cooperative  study programs. View Cooperative Study Programs What you will find at KIT What matters to us is your skills and your goals. Whether you’re pursuing vocational training or a cooperative study program, You will work on real projects, help shape the future, and continue to grow. At the same time, you will have room for everything that matters to you Top-Notch Training and Opportunities Hands-on experience, projects, and in-depth knowledge: Your path to a career with a future. . Team Spirit and Respect Learning as a team, support from day one, and respectful collaboration Getting Started and Advancing Whether permanent employment or further development, we will support you every step of the way. What You Bring to the Table and What You Will Get in Return You must have at least a secondary school diploma (for some professions, a basic school diploma is sufficient) or, for a cooperative study program, a university of applied sciences entrance qualification or a high school diploma/A levels (Abitur). You should be curious, a team player, and willing to take on responsibility. All applications are welcome – we provide language support and recognize international credentials  . A Glimpse into the Training Program Vocational Training on TikTok (in German) Vocational Training on Instagram (in German) Apply now On our training page, you will find open positions for vocational training and cooperative study. Apply online and start building your future with us. Open Positions KIT You may also be interested in: Working Environment Diversity Work Culture Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
