Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Application Process Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Application Process FAQ Our Application Process Whether in research, engineering, or administration, your career at KIT begins with a structured and supportive application process. We place the utmost importance on transparency, accountability, and fairness, ensuring that everyone is treated fairly and with respect. We look forward to receiving your application! Stages of the Application Process We will guide you every step of the way, from your initial interest to your first day on the job, so you can focus on what matters most: Your individual strengths and your motivation. Preparing Your Application Learn About Us You want to know what sets KIT apart? Then get to know us as a hub for excellence in research, teaching, and innovation, and discover the areas where you can make a difference: Large-scale research, IT services, laboratories, and administration. Find the Right Position Use the job search and filter by category, location, or target group. The fastest and most accessible way is to apply online via the KIT Job Portal . Your Application Résumé – Short and Clear In reverse chronological order, no more than two pages, and easy to read. Highlight relevant experience (e.g., lab internship, software project, shift management in customer service, or committee work). A photo is optional. Tips for your résumé Cover Letter (Optional) If you wish to write a cover letter, it should be tailored specifically to the position and include additional information not already listed in your résumé. Go for It! If you don't meet all the requirements in the job posting, apply anyway if you cover most of them. Motivation, a willingness to learn, and your potential count. At KIT, we support your professional and personal development, e.g., through continued education offerings, qualification programs, or targeted onboarding. After You Apply Review of Your Documents Once the application deadline has passed, we will check your documents against the job requirements. Invitation If your profile stands out compared to other applications, we will invite you to an interview in a timely manner, including the date, location or online link, and instructions on how to prepare. Face-to-face Interview Your Preparation Think about the experience and strengths you bring to the table. What motivates you? Why do you want to join KIT? Why are you specifically interested in this position at KIT? We would like to hear about your motivation and expectations. Procedure In person or online. Depending on the position, in addition to managers, team members and, if applicable, representatives from Human Resources, the Staff Council, and Representatives of Disabled Employees will also participate. Employment Contract Offer Once you have successfully completed the selection process, you will receive a contract offer. Your HR contact person will coordinate all further details with you. Getting Started Together We will guide you through every step of the process, from your start date to preparing for your first day. FAQ Answers to the most frequently asked questions about documents, deadlines, the application process, and interviews – concise and easy to follow. View FAQs You may also be interested in: Get Started Diversity Benefits Working Environment Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-05-06 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
