      "description": "FAQ | KIT KIT - Karlsruhe Institute of Technology image/svg+xml Karlsruhe Institute of Technology skip navigation Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT de search search KIT Start KIT KIT Profile Start KIT Profile Profile Vision Excellence Start KIT Profile Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Equal Opportunities and Diversity Sustainability Data and Facts Start KIT Profile Data and Facts Data and Facts Rankings Organization Start KIT Organization Organization Management Bodies and Committees Start KIT Organization Bodies and Committees Bodies and Committees Supervisory Board Executive Board Heads of Divisions KIT Senate Convention Staff Representation Students Union Divisions Start KIT Organization Divisions Divisions Institutes KIT Departments HGF Programs KIT Centers Administration and Infrastructure Project Management Agency Karlsruhe People Start KIT People People Personalities History Top-level Researchers Start KIT People Top-level Researchers Top-level Researchers Alexander von Humboldt Foundation AvH European Research Council German Research Foundation Getting Involved Start KIT Getting Involved Getting Involved KIT GIVING KIT Foundation Sponsoring KIT Alumni KFG Media Start KIT Media Media Press Releases Start KIT Media Press Releases Press Releases PI 2026 Archive Press Releases News Start KIT Media News News News 2026 Highlight Topics Newly Appointed Annual Report Publications Campus Life Start KIT Campus Life Campus Life 200 Years of KIT KIT for All Campus Tours Events Start KIT Campus Life Events Events Events Calendar Locations Start KIT Locations Locations Interactive Campus Map Maps for Download Topics Start Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Studies Start Studies Studies Prior to Studies Start Studies Prior to Studies Prior to Studies Degree Programs Application Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe International Students During Studies Start Studies During Studies During Studies Student Organizations Intranet After Studies Start Studies After Studies After Studies Organizational Matters Master and Doctorate Starting Work Staying in Touch KIT Departments Advice and Help Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Start Studies Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living and Learning in Karlsruhe Living in Karlsruhe Learning at the KIT Transportation Research Start Research Research Topics Start Research Topics Topics Elementary and Astroparticle Physics Energy Health Information Climate and Environment Materials Mathematics Humans and Technology Mobility Excellence Start Research Excellence Excellence University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence Helmholtz Programs Research Networks Start Research Research Networks Research Networks Collaborative Research Centers DFG Research Units Young Scientists Start Research Young Scientists Young Scientists Doctorate Start Research Young Scientists Doctorate Doctorate Doing a Doctorate at KIT Doctoral Programs Postdoc Phase Paths to Professorship Start Research Young Scientists Paths to Professorship Paths to Professorship Young Investigator Group Preparation Program KIT-Nachwuchsgruppe KIT Associate Fellow Tenure-track Professorship Research Infrastructures Security Research Scientific Integrity Innovation Start Innovation Innovation Technology Transfer Cooperation Innovation in Academic Education and Research Starting a Business Career Start Career Career Working at KIT Start Career Working at KIT Working at KIT Work Culture Diversity Benefits Working Environment KIT for International Talent Get Started Start Career Get Started Get Started Science Infrastructure Administration Vocational Training and Cooperative Study Programs Students Application Process Start Career Application Process Application Process FAQ Jobs Startpage Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet search search Startpage Career Application Process FAQ Karlsruhe Institute of Technology KIT Topics Studies Research Innovation Career Career Working at KIT KIT for International Talent Get Started Application Process Jobs Application Process FAQ FAQ FAQs Regarding Your Application You Have Questions? We provide you with clear answers and offer accessible support right from the start. In our FAQs about applying to KIT, you will find everything you need to know about our application process, the requirements, and your next steps. General Information Regarding Your Application Which Form of Application Does KIT Prefer? Please use our online application via our Application Portal whenever possible. Applications via email or in writing will be only accepted in exceptional cases. How Long Does It Take to Fill Out the Online Application Form? Entering your information will usually take five to ten minutes. What Are the Technical Requirements for the Online Application? PDFs are ideal. Word, PPT, JPG, PNG, and GIF files are also acceptable. Individual files should be no larger than 10 MB, and the entire application should not exceed 20 MB. For optimal performance, we recommend using a modern web browser such as Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Microsoft Edge. What Documents Should My Application Include? Your application should include at least a current résumé as well as relevant certificates and supporting documents (e.g., academic degrees, employment references). How Long Does the Application Process Take? The application process, starting with the submission of your application and ending with a potential offer of employment, can vary depending on the position, the volume of applications, and the review process. However, you should generally expect to hear back within two to three months. Please note: The review process does not begin until after the application deadline has passed. Submitting Your Application Who Should I Send My Application To? Please send your application to the contact person from the department or Human Resources listed in the job posting (see the contact information in the respective posting). How Can I Get in Touch with a Contact Person Directly? You can find the contact information directly in the respective job posting. The relevant contact persons are listed there along with their email addresses and phone numbers. Can I Make Changes or Additions to My Application After Submitting It? Yes. If you applied through the online portal, you can add to or update your application materials during the application period, but only via email and not online via the application portal. If you have any questions, please contact the Human Resources (PSE) representative listed in the job posting. Will I Be Sent a Confirmation of Receipt? Yes. After submitting your online application, you will automatically receive a confirmation via email. For applications submitted via email or in writing, you will also receive a confirmation of receipt via email. Can I Withdraw My Application? Yes. Please inform the contact person from the department or the Human Resources (PSE) if you wish to withdraw your application. How Accessible is the Application Process? KIT is actively committed to accessibility and equal opportunity. If you need assistance with the application process, please feel free to contact the Representatives of Disabled Employees or the Human Resources (PSE) contact person listed in the job posting. Special Application Situations Can I Apply for More Than One Position at the Same Time? Yes, that is possible. Please tailor your application specifically to each position. Are There Job Openings for International Applicants? Yes. We assist you with the recognition of foreign degrees and, through our Welcome Service , offer help with questions regarding visas, residency, and work permits. How Do We Handle Foreign Degrees? Your degree will be reviewed to determine if it corresponds to a German qualification. If necessary, we will guide you through the recognition process. In Which Language Can I Apply? Applications may be submitted in German or English. We welcome applicants from all linguistic backgrounds. What Language Skills Are Required? The required language skills depend on the specific position. Generally, a solid command of German or English is expected; details can be found in the respective job posting. Selection Process How Does the Selection Process Work? After the application deadline, we review your application documents for completeness and relevant qualifications. Candidates who are suitable for the position and stand out from other applicants will be invited to a personal interview. In some cases, a second round of interviews may follow. How Can I Prepare for the Interview? Learn about KIT, the position, and the department. Think about what motivates you and what you bring to the table. Asking your own questions demonstrates your interest. How Can I Track the Status of My Application? There is currently no publicly available application tracking system. If you have any questions, please contact the Human Resources (PSE) representative listed in the job posting directly. Will My Travel Expenses for Job Interviews Be Reimbursed? Unfortunately, as a general rule, no: Travel expenses for job interviews at KIT cannot be reimbursed. We appreciate your understanding. What Happens If My Application Is Incomplete? If important documents are missing, the Human Resources Business Unit will contact you. Please make sure your application is complete and accurate to avoid delays or disqualification on formal grounds. If you still wish to submit additional documents, you can email them to the contact person from the Human Resources Business Unit (PSE) listed in the job posting. What Happens to My Data After I Apply? Your data will be processed strictly in accordance with legal requirements and automatically deleted after the statutory retention periods expire, provided you are not hired. How Long Will My Data Be Stored If I Am Not Hired? Your data will be automatically deleted 100 days after the conclusion of the process in accordance with applicable data protection regulations. Apply Now The KIT Job Portal provides an overview of all open positions in technology, infrastructure, and administration. Discover new opportunities and apply now. Job Offers You may also be interested in: Application Process Work Culture Benefits Get Started Contact Karlsruhe Institute of Technology Phone: +49 721 608-0 Fax: +49 721 608-44290 Staff Search Address Media Press Releases Contact for Media Applying Jobs Degree Programs Trainee Positions Doctorate Visiting How to reach the KIT Campus Map Events KIT-Shop Instagram Profile Facebook Profile Youtube Profile Mastodon Profile LinkedIn Profile last change:\n                        2026-07-01 KIT – The University in the Helmholtz Association Home Plain Language Legals Privacy Policy Accessibility Sitemap Intranet KIT"
    },
